overview.text:
Designed with working professionals in mind, this two-year degree program offers the opportunity to obtain a high-quality master's degree. Our cohort-based model supports collaborative inquiry in the context of carefully structured and guided explorations of educational theory and practice (18-24 students).
Drawing on developments in the field of practitioner inquiry over the past two decades, the program will help you build capacities and expertise in the following ways:
Situating yourself as an educator within particular educational theories and traditions of practice;
Developing skills and experience in the design and implementation of classroom inquiry;
Gathering a variety of evidence on which to base pedagogical and curricular decisions;
Synthesizing and representing your learning to a community of practitioner-inquirers through a comprehensive examination (a written paper and summative presentation).
B.C. K-12 Educators:
You may be eligible for a TQS category upgrade upon successful completion of the program.
